  "result": "Excellent! All 209 tests pass (30 new payment terms tests added). Payment terms are now fully integrated:\n\n**src/invoices.js updates:**\n- `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` - helper function supporting:\n  - **NET14** - due 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30** - due 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - **EOM** - due on the last day of the issue date's month\n- `createInvoice()` now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Validates terms against allowed values, returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms\n- Calculates and stores `dueDate` on invoice object\n\n**src/errors.js:**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code\n\n**test/terms.test.js (30 comprehensive tests):**\n- Default NET30 and explicit term acceptance\n- Invalid term rejection with proper error messages\n- NET14 due date calculations (regular, month/year boundaries)\n- NET30 due date calculations (regular, month/year boundaries, last day of month)\n- EOM due date calculations (all month lengths, leap years, edge cases)\n- Invoice structure validation\n- Edge cases: 1st of month, multiple SKUs, whitespace handling\n\nAll date arithmetic is UTC-based using the existing `addDays()` function, maintaining project consistency.",
